---
name: button-group
type: registry:ui
title: Button Group
description: A container that groups related buttons together with consistent styling.
dependencies:
  - tailwind-variants
registryDependencies:
  - separator
files:
  - path: registry/items/components/button-group/index.ts
    type: registry:ui
    target: '~/components/button-group/index.ts'
  - path: registry/items/components/button-group/button-group.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: '~/components/button-group/button-group.svelte'
  - path: registry/items/components/button-group/button-group.variants.ts
    type: registry:ui
    target: '~/components/button-group/button-group.variants.ts'
  - path: registry/items/components/button-group/button-group-text.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: '~/components/button-group/button-group-text.svelte'
  - path: registry/items/components/button-group/button-group-separator.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: '~/components/button-group/button-group-separator.svelte'
---

Use button group to cluster related actions. Set `orientation` to `horizontal` or `vertical`.
Pair with `ButtonGroup.Separator` for non-outline button variants.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import * as ButtonGroup from '~/components/button-group';
	import { Button } from '~/components/button';
</script>

<ButtonGroup.Root aria-label="Actions">
	<Button variant="outline">Archive</Button>
	<Button variant="secondary">Report</Button>
	<Button>Snooze</Button>
</ButtonGroup.Root>
```
